Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.60,0:00:45.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now suppose this stripe is 100 km from the ridge and 5 million years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.60,0:00:48.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then the half-spreading rate is 100 km ÷ 5 million years,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.60,0:00:49.95,Eq,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(960,64)\fad(250,0)}100 km ÷ 5 Myr = 2 cm/yr
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.45,0:00:49.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is 2 cm per year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.15,0:00:55.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the seafloor works like a tape recorder, logging every flip of Earth's magnetic field.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.65,0:01:00.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Read the stripes, and we can measure motion slower than your fingernails grow.
